> Through the Marine Resources Initiative, Auspatious is working alongside Geoscience Australia to deliver Earth observation expertise, practical training, and cloud-based data infrastructure to partner agencies across Southeast Asia. Our role includes capacity development, data processing, hands-on training, and sustained mentoring, building real, lasting capabilities with teams across the region.

We began our contribution by processing coastal and marine datasets for Vietnam and the Philippines, to support marine spatial planning and resource management. This groundwork informed a training workshop we led in the Philippines, introducing local teams to Earth observation science and satellite-derived coastal monitoring tools and techniques.

<figure class="not-prose my-8">
  <enhanced:img src={datacube} alt="Datacube" sizes="100vw" class="w-full" />
  <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm opacity-70">Open Data Cube</figcaption>
</figure>

We're also working closely with the national Geospatial Information Agenc in Indonesia, Badan Informasi Geospasial (BIG). In Bogor, we ran a Coastal Earth Observation Science workshop, introducing participants to satellite-based coastal monitoring using Digital Earth products. A follow-on workshop in Sydney deepened the BIG team's skills in large-scale data processing using the cloud.

<figure class="not-prose my-8">
  <enhanced:img src={workshop2} alt="Indonesia Workshop" sizes="100vw" class="w-full" />
  <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm opacity-70">Indonesia Workshop, 2025</figcaption>
</figure>

This work provides Auspatious with an opportunity to share knowledge, but more importantly, to empower people to deliver their own analysis using a Digital Earth platform that they maintain and use. The team was previously limited in the scale of analyses they could run and now they have the capability to run national analysis.
